[Music]  late stage trials of one potential  coronavirus vaccine are resuming in at  least two countries  after they were put on hold when a  participant developed symptoms of a rare  neurological disorder  the oxford astrazeneca vaccine is one of  the leading candidates in clinical tests  dr ashish jaws dean of brown university  school of public health  he joins us from providence rhode island  to discuss good to see you dr zha  and congratulations it seems like you  have a new position two weeks ago you  were at harvard now you're at brown  we know you're in high demand we're glad  you're here with us this morning  really good to see you good morning good  morning thank you for having me on  so it was put on hold over i mean it's  resuming overseas it's still on hold  here  do you read anything to that about why  it's not why isn't it resumed here in  this country  yeah so um thank you again for having me  on you know this is  confusing and one of the things that's  not been clear is exactly what happened  that caused the pause and why things  have resumed and i think it's really  important  for astrazeneca and the researchers to  be very transparent with the people of  the united states of great britain of  everybody  about exactly what happened so we can  all have more confidence in the process  because we all we all are very nervous  everybody wants a vaccine but we want it  to be safe and it seems to be such a  political hot potato why do you think  it's so important that they are  transparent let us know all the details  and why wouldn't they let us know the  details  yeah so first of all absolutely we're  all anxious for a vaccine i'm anxious  for a vaccine we all want one but we  need it for it we need for it to be safe  and effective  you know in general with no under normal  times  all this stuff is not always disclosed  it is eventually disclosed to the fda  but these are not normal times  and therefore given how much attention  we're all paying  i think it's critical for the  investigators to make all of this stuff  completely public  dr shah the ceo of pfizer who was on  face the nation yesterday said there's  more than a 60  chance the company will know by the end  of october  whether its vaccine works what do you  make of that and what could that mean  yeah so i've been really optimistic  about a timeline that we will have  vaccines that are found to be safe and  effective this fall  but we don't know what is motivating him  to say that i think again one of the  things that i have called for and others  have called for  is that these vaccine manufacturers  should absolutely  make their protocols and their research  and their statistical plans  all public so we can understand what's  motivating him to say that what's  underlying that assessment and without  that it's very difficult dr john if  if that does happen though if if we get  a successful vaccine by the fall how  long would it be  before people actually get vaccinated  yeah  so if you think about it we're going to  have to make hundreds of millions of  doses now some of those already being  made  but even after we have got them made  it's going to take many months to  distribute them  you know i always say vaccines don't  save lives vaccinations do and it will  take  us well into 2021 before a majority of  americans get a vaccine  you know the president said we have  rounded a corner on this corona virus  that's one school of thought dr anthony  fauci  says listen we may not be back to normal  to the end of next year  where do you stand what are your  thoughts  yeah so i unfortunately agree with dr  fauci on this  um where we have not rounded a corner i  think we're going to have some very hard  months ahead  i do believe 2021 will be better and by  spring to summer of 21  i think life will be meaningfully better  in many parts of the country  uh but we still have many months to go  and i'm worried that if we you know sort  of take our eye off the prize  we can end up seeing a lot of infections  and what do you need to see to let  people know that  it's okay to take the vaccine what do  you want to see  yeah i want to see data and i want to  see data on both effectiveness  and i want to see large enough people a  number of people in the trials and a  diverse enough number of people  before i know that it's safe for me my  family my elderly parents  and what i would recommend to others so  we really have to see the evidence and  data before we make a decision about  whether it's safe and effective  all right dr john thank you we'll be in  touch really good to have you here today

